[h1]Quick Start: Your First TooltipLib Provider[/h1]

Want to add content to PZ tooltips without the metatable juggling? Here's everything you need.

[h2]Step 1: Depend on TooltipLib[/h2]

In your mod's [b]mod.info[/b], add:
[code]require=TooltipLib[/code]

[h2]Step 2: Register a Provider[/h2]

Create a Lua file in [b]media/lua/client/[/b] (tooltip code is client-only):

[code]
require "TooltipLib/Core"

TooltipLib.registerProvider({
    id          = "MyMod_WeaponDamage",
    target      = "item",
    enabled     = TooltipLib.Filters.weapon,
    cacheable   = true,
    description = "Weapon damage stats",
    callback    = function(ctx)
        local item = ctx.item
        local minDmg = item:getMinDamage()
        local maxDmg = item:getMaxDamage()

        ctx:addKeyValue("Min Damage:", string.format("%.1f", minDmg))
        ctx:addKeyValue("Max Damage:", string.format("%.1f", maxDmg))
    end,
})
[/code]

That's it. No hooking ISToolTipInv. No pcall wrapping. No layout management. Your content appears below vanilla stats, columns aligned, alongside every other mod's content.

[h2]What Each Field Does[/h2]

[list]
[*] [b]id[/b] — Unique string. Namespace it to your mod (e.g. "MyMod_Feature").
[*] [b]target[/b] — Which tooltip surface: "item", "itemSlot", "object", "skill", "vehicle", or "recipe".
[*] [b]enabled[/b] — Filter function. Without it, your callback runs for ALL items. Use built-in filters or write your own.
[*] [b]cacheable[/b] — Set true and the framework records your ctx calls once, then replays them for free on subsequent frames. Big perf win.
[*] [b]description[/b] — Human-readable name. Shows up in Mod Options as a player-facing toggle. Always set this.
[*] [b]callback[/b] — Where you add content. Gets a context object (ctx) with methods like addKeyValue, addProgress, addLabel, etc.
[/list]

[h2]What You Can Add[/h2]

[code]
local C = TooltipLib.Colors

-- Colored label
ctx:addLabel("Legendary", C.GOLD)

-- Key-value pair with aligned columns
ctx:addKeyValue("Damage:", "+15%", C.WHITE, C.GREEN)

-- Progress bar (0.0 to 1.0)
ctx:addProgress("Durability:", 0.75, nil, C.BLUE)

-- Auto-colored integers (+N green, -N red)
ctx:addInteger("Critical:", 15, true)

-- Auto-colored percentages
ctx:addPercentage("Crit Chance:", 0.15, 0, true)  -- "+15%"

-- Float with decimal control
ctx:addFloat("Speed:", 0.35, 1, true)  -- "+0.4"

-- Section header (auto-spacer above)
ctx:addHeader("-- Bonuses --", C.GOLD)

-- Blank line / horizontal rule
ctx:addSpacer()
ctx:addDivider()

-- Word-wrapped text block
ctx:addText("A long description that wraps nicely.", C.GRAY)
[/code]

[h2]Detail Mode (Shift Key)[/h2]

Don't clutter tooltips. Gate extra info behind the detail key:

[code]
callback = function(ctx)
    ctx:addKeyValue("Damage:", "15")  -- always visible

    if ctx.detail then
        ctx:addKeyValue("Base Damage:", "10")
        ctx:addKeyValue("Bonus:", "+5")
    end
end,
[/code]

Or hide the entire provider until Shift is held:
[code]
detailOnly = true,
[/code]
